BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (    # The Tale of the River Eternal) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (    In the time before time, two villages stood on opposite banks of the River Eternal. The Upst) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      ream Village received fresh water each day, while the Downstream Village struggled with dr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (    The Water-Keeper of the Upstream Village faced a choice: hoard the precious water or release) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (       it downstream. The spirits had blessed the water with a peculiar magic-whatever was sent ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      downstream would triple in abundance as it flowed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (    The first Water-Keeper, moved by compassion, sent one-third of their water downstream. The s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      pirits blessed this generosity, and the water multiplied. The grateful Downstream Village,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (       now flourishing, sent back gifts of grain and fish-sometimes equal to what they'd receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      d, sometimes more, sometimes less.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    Over seasons, a rhythm emerged. When Water-Keepers sent generously, the downstream village p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      rospered and returned abundance. When they withheld from fear, both villages suffered-for ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      the magic only worked through trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    The wisest Water-Keepers learned that sending freely created prosperity for all. Even when r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      eturns varied like the phases of the moon, the act of giving itself invited reciprocity. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      he river taught them: abundance flows to those who trust it to flow, and communities flour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      ish when each considers the other's needs as important as their own.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    Thus the villages thrived, forever linked by the River Eternal.) Tj ET
